The [[2027 New South Wales state election]] will be held on 13 March 2027 to elect all 93 seats of the [[New South Wales Legislative Assembly|Legislative Assembly]], as well as 21 out of the 42 [[New South Wales Legislative Council|Legislative Council]] seats. 

Nominations for candidates are scheduled to close at 12:00 PM AEST on 24 February, 2027, and the [[NSW Electoral Commission]] is expected to declare the nominations the following day.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2027 NSW State election |url=https://elections.nsw.gov.au/elections/state-elections/2027-nsw-state-election |access-date=2026-08-17 |website=elections.nsw.gov.au |language=en-au}}</ref>

== Retiring members ==
The following members announced that they will not be contesting the 2027 election:

=== Labor ===

* [[Hugh McDermott (politician)|Hugh McDermott]] MP ([[Electoral district of Prospect|Prospect]]) – announced 1 October 2026<ref>{{Cite web |last=Maddison |first=Max |date=2026-10-01 |title=Veteran MP resigns as NSW Labor HQ targets male backbenchers |url=https://www.smh.com.au/politics/nsw/veteran-mp-resigns-as-nsw-labor-hq-targets-male-backbenchers-20261001-p6121v.html |access-date=2026-10-01 |website=The Sydney Morning Herald |language=en}}</ref>

=== Liberal ===
*[[James Griffin (Australian politician)|James Griffin]] MP ([[Electoral district of Manly|Manly]]) – announced 2 September 2026<ref>{{Cite web |last=Vince |first=Avi |date=2026-09-02 |title=Member for Manly, James Griffin, announces retirement |url=https://manlyobserver.com.au/member-for-manly-james-griffin-announces-retirement/ |access-date=2026-09-11 |website=Manly Observer |language=en-US}}</ref> 
*[[Alister Henskens]] MP ([[Electoral district of Wahroonga|Wahroonga]]) – announced 11 September 2026<ref>{{Cite web |last=McSweeney |first=Jessica |date=2026-09-11 |title=Kellie Sloane loses second senior frontbencher in as many weeks |url=https://www.smh.com.au/politics/nsw/kellie-sloane-loses-second-senior-frontbencher-in-as-many-weeks-20260911-p60wm4.html |access-date=2026-09-11 |website=The Sydney Morning Herald |language=en}}</ref> 
*[[Mark Taylor (Australian politician)|Mark Taylor]] MP ([[Electoral district of Winston Hills|Winston Hills]]) – announced 8 July 2026<ref>{{Cite web |last=Dodds |first=Troy |date=2026-07-08 |title=Winston Hills MP Mark Taylor won't contest the 2027 State Election - Parra News - Parramatta's Independent Voice |url=https://www.parranews.com.au/2026/07/winston-hills-mp-mark-taylor-wont-contest-the-2027-state-election/ |access-date=2026-09-11 |language=en-US}}</ref> 
=== Greens ===
*[[Tamara Smith]] MP ([[Electoral district of Ballina|Ballina]]) – announced 1 May 2026<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bruem |first=Rod |date=2026-05-01 |title=Ballina Greens MP Tamara Smith to exit politics after three terms |url=https://ballinanewsdaily.com.au/2026/05/ballina-greens-mp-tamara-smith-to-exit-politics-after-three-terms/ |access-date=2026-09-11 |website=Ballina News Daily |language=en-AU}}</ref>

